# In-progress benchmark checkpoints. tools/benchmark_quality_reference.py writes one after
# every problem so a killed run can resume, and deletes it once the real artifact exists. It
# is working state, not a result: committing one mid-run records a measurement that is
# neither finished nor labelled as unfinished.
*.json.partial
*.json.partial.tmp

# Xcode / SwiftPM
*.xcuserdata
DerivedData/
*.xcframework/

# Secrets / credentials (never commit these)
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
!*.pub.key
id_rsa
id_rsa.*
id_ed25519
id_ed25519.*
credentials.json
*.pfx
*.p12
secrets.yaml
secrets.yml
secrets.json

# Compiled Metal libraries. Build outputs — scripts/build_xcframework.sh, build_ios_app.sh and
# scripts/run_quality_benchmark.sh all write them — and dangerous when committed: the engine
# prefers a .metallib that exports every kernel name it needs, and a stale one does. The
# committed transformer_ops.metallib predated three kernel fixes in its source, so a run that
# found it ran the unfixed kernels while CI's name-only check passed. Without the binary the
# engine compiles the .metal source, which is always current.
antigravity-engine/src/shaders/*.metallib
